fied DnaK\nL413@P4: interactors (eight essential proteins), such as excision nuclease\nL414@P4: subunit A (uvrA) (Table S3). The extent of aggregation correlated\nL415@P4: strongly with enrichment on DnaK (Table S3).\nL416@P4: These findings demonstrate that a subset of DnaK interactors\nL417@P4: are specifically dependent on the DnaK system in vivo. These\nL418@P4: proteins tend to be degraded or aggregate in DKJ cells, even\nL419@P4: at a growth temperature of 30\u0003C, where the loss of DnaK is\nL420@P4: otherwise well compensated.\nL421@P4: DnaK Interacts with Newly Synthesized and Preexistent\nL422@P4: Proteins\nL423@P4: To determine whether proteins interact with DnaK only during\nL582@P6: \u00011.4-fold in DT/KHis cells; see Table S6D below.) The additional\nL583@P6: A\nL584@P6: D\nL585@P6: 641 357\nL586@P6: (672)\nL587@P6: DnaK\u0002interactors\nL588@P6: (998)\nL589@P6: DnaK-interactors\nL590@P6: in ΔT/K cells\nL591@P6: B C\nL592@P6: Molecular mass (kDa)\nL593@P6: Frequency (%)\nL594@P6: 0\nL595@P6: 10\nL596@P6: 20\nL597@P6: 30\nL598@P6: 40\nL599@P6: Isoelectric point (pI)\nL600@P6: Frequency (%)\nL601@P6: <5\nL602@P6: 5-6\nL603@P6: 6-7\nL604@P6: 7-8\nL605@P6: 8-9\nL606@P6: 9-10\nL607@P6: 10-11\nL608@P6: >11\nL609@P6: 0\nL610@P6: 10\nL611@P6: 20\nL612@P6: 30\nL613@P6: 40\nL614@P6: E\nL615@P6: Time (min)\nL616@P6: WT + deoxycholate 0.1%\nL617@P6: WT + vancomycin 50 μg/ml\nL618@P6: MC4100 ΔT/K\nL619@P6: MC4100 WT\nL620@P6: ΔT/K + deoxycholate 0.1%\nL621@P6: ΔT/K + vancomycin 50 μg/ml\nL622@P6: 39 1 2 25 67\nL623@P6: Increased on\nL624@P6: DnaK in ΔT/K\nL625@P6: (71)\nL626@P6: Increased in\nL627@P6: ΔT/K proteome\nL628@P6: (27)\nL629@P6: Decreased in\nL630@P6: ΔT/K proteome\nL631@P6: (40)\nL632@P6: 0 50 100 150 200 250 300 350 400\nL633@P6: 0.0\nL634@P6: 0.5\nL635@P6: 1.0\nL636@P6: 1.5\nL637@P6: 2.0\nL638@P6: 2.5\nL639@P6: 3.0\nL640@P6: 3.5\nL641@P6: OD600nm\nL642@P6: secretory\nL643@P6: proteins\nL644@P6: chaperones;\nL645@P6: proteases\nL646@P6: ribosomal &\